  "claim": "Henricus Antonius \"Han\" van Meegeren presented a forged sword to a military leader who was the recipient of Pour le Mérite.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Han van Meegeren. Sentence: Henricus Antonius \"Han\" van Meegeren (] ; 10 October 1889 – 30 December 1947) was a Dutch painter and portraitist and is considered to be one of the most ingenious art forgers of the 20th century.\nPage: Han van Meegeren. Sentence: Despite his life of crime, van Meegeren became a national hero after World War Two when it was revealed that he had sold a forged painting to Reichsmarschall Hermann Göring during the Nazi Occupation of the Netherlands.\nPage: Hermann Göring. Sentence: Hermann Wilhelm Göring (or Goering; ] ; 12 January 1893 – 15 October 1946) was a German political and military leader as well as one of the most powerful figures in the Nazi Party (NSDAP) that ruled Germany from 1933 to 1945.\nPage: Hermann Göring. Sentence: A veteran World War I fighter pilot ace, he was a recipient of the \"Pour le Mérite\".",
